 "note": "Cloud A/B, A/A with both arms as pages of ONE browser, the arrangement the tool no longer uses: `npm run perf:ab -- --aa --shots cruise-horizon`, 2026-10-12 08:34-08:46 UTC, same host as perf-ab-aa-cruise-horizon-2026-10-12.json, with an earlier revision of the tool (8 rounds; it also timed the GPU process's CPU time as `gpuProcess`, since dropped). Both arms are one build. The timings agree, but the frames do not: 279,159 pixels differ, by up to 22 levels in 255, all of them water. In one arm GlobalHeightPyramid.bakeHorizon awaited a compute pipeline through Babylon's dispatchWhenReady, which stops polling after 3,000 tries without settling, so that arm never published the horizon field and its water lost its terrain occlusion. docs/PERFORMANCE.md, 'Cloud A/B', 'A browser per arm'.",
